{"tool_name":"pupl","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"pupl","home":"http://github.com/kinleyid/pupl","license":"Other","summary":"An open-source tool for processing pupillometry data.","addition_date":"2022-05-17T20:39:52.431989Z","last_update_date":"2022-05-17T20:40:28.400887Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:pupl","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Isaac Kinley"},{"name":"Yarden Levy"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/kinleyid/PuPl/blob/master/manual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sorting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3802"}]}],"name":"PuPl","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.3758/S13428-021-01717-Z","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Psychonomic Society, Inc.We present PuPl (Pu pillometry P ipel iner), an Octave-compatible library of Matlab functions for processing pupillometry data with an easy-to-use graphical user interface (GUI). PuPl\u2019s preprocessing tools include blink correction, data smoothing, and gaze correction. PuPl can also define and sort trials, and segment data to isolate event-related pupil dilation responses. PuPl\u2019s flexible tabular export tools enable a wide variety of statistical analyses. Furthermore, PuPl can translate GUI interactions into a Matlab script, enabling easy creation and reconfiguration of reusable data processing pipelines. Finally, PuPl is designed to be extensible, and users can easily contribute functionality as best practices for pupillometry evolve. Here we demonstrate PuPl by replicating published results using publicly available data. PuPl can be downloaded from github.com/kinleyid/pupl.","authors":[{"name":"Kinley I."},{"name":"Levy Y."}],"date":"2021-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Behavior Research Methods","title":"PuPl: an open-source tool for processing p